  "priorExpiration": "2000-03-31",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 2606.05 Application for a State License to Sell or Market Permissible Fireworks.\n\n(a) Upon issuance of a local permit to sell permissible fireworks by a municipality, a person may apply for a state license to sell or market permissible fireworks.\n\n(b) Each applicant for a state license to sell or market permissible fireworks shall complete and submit the application form, DSSP 262P, “Application for License to Sell Permissible Fireworks”, effective July, 2014.\n\n(c) Each corporate or partnership applicant shall include the following along with form DSSP 262P:\n\n(1) A certificate of authority or certificate of vote indicating that the person filling out the application is authorized by the corporation or partnership to bind the corporation or partnership;\n\n(2) Disclosure required by RSA 160-C:3, II-f and II-g; and\n\n(3) If an applicant is intending to use a trade name, evidence that demonstrates that the trade name is currently registered in New Hampshire, pursuant to RSA 160-C:3, II-d.\n\n(d) Each applicant for a state license to sell permissible fireworks shall also submit the applicable fee pursuant to RSA 160-C;3, VII.\n\n(e) Prior to the issuance of a state license to sell permissible fireworks, the commissioner shall inspect the applicant’s business and storage area(s) to ensure compliance with all applicable fire safety codes, building codes, zoning codes, and the requirements of local ordinances.\n\nSource. #5752, eff 12-2-93; ss by INTERIM #7140, eff 12-2-99, EXPIRED: 3-31-00\n\nNew. #7905, eff 6-24-03; ss by #8519, eff 12-16-05; ss by #10784, eff 2-13-15",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c2600.html"
